{"id":14986,"artist":"Johnny Mercer / Harold Arlen","title":"ONE FOR MY BABY (AND ONE MORE FOR THE ROAD)","lyrics_plain":"It's quarter to three,\nthere's no one in the place\nexcept you and me.\nSo, set 'em up, Joe,\nI got a little story\nyou ought to know.\nWe're drinkin', my friend,\nto the end\nof a brief episode.\nMake it one for my baby\nand one more for the road.\nI got the routine,\nput another nickel\nin the machine.\nFeelin' so bad,\ncan't you make the music\neasy and sad?\nI could tell you a lot,\nbut you got to be\ntrue to your code.\nMake it one for my baby\nand one more for the road.\nYou'd never know it,\nbut Buddy, I'm a kind of poet\nand I got a lotta things I'd like to say.\nAnd when I'm gloomy,\nwon't you listen to me\ntill it's talked away?\nWell, that's how it goes,\nand Joe, I know you're gettin'\nanxious to close.\nAnd thanks for the cheer,\nI hope you didn't mind\nmy bendin' your ear.\nBut this torch that I've found\ngotta be drowned\nor it soon might explode.\nSo, make it one for my baby\nand one more for the road,\nthe long, that long, it's long.","lyrics_synced":"[00:16.68] It's quarter to three,\n[00:20.18] there's no one in the place\n[00:23.66] except you and me.\n[00:30.62] So, set 'em up, Joe,\n[00:33.95] I got a little story\n[00:37.90] you ought to know.\n[00:44.55] We're drinkin', my friend,\n[00:48.87] to the end\n[00:51.25] of a brief episode.\n[00:57.34] Make it one for my baby\n[01:02.80] and one more for the road.\n[01:12.29] I got the routine,\n[01:16.15] put another nickel\n[01:20.19] in the machine.\n[01:26.61] Feelin' so bad,\n[01:30.09] can't you make the music\n[01:33.23] easy and sad?\n[01:39.94] I could tell you a lot,\n[01:43.42] but you got to be\n[01:47.09] true to your code.\n[01:53.00] Make it one for my baby\n[01:58.14] and one more for the road.\n[02:08.08] You'd never know it,\n[02:10.66] but Buddy, I'm a kind of poet\n[02:14.21] and I got a lotta things I'd like to say.\n[02:21.92] And when I'm gloomy,\n[02:25.